            },
            "label": {
              "000001T8": "Proportion of gainfully employed (new definition 2019)",
              "0000026C": "Proportion of business operators of gainfully employed persons (new def. 2019)",
              "000001TC": "Proportion of persons registered as unemployed, percent",
              "0000026B": "Proportion of persons openly unemployed, percent",
              "0000026D": "Proportion of job-seekers in programmes with activity support, percent",
              "0000026E": "Proportion of long-term unemployed, percent",
              "0000026F": "Proportion of persons still gainfully employed after a year (new def. 2019)",
              "0000026G": "Prop. of persons who are still business operators after a year (new def. 2019)",
              "0000026I": "Proportion of persons in managerial positions, percent",
              "0000026J": "Proportion with post-secondary education, occupational areas 2–3. SSYK, percent",
              "0000026K": "Proportion with post-secondary education working at qual. level 3–4, percent"
            },
            "note": {
              "000001T8": [
                "The numerator consists of the number of gainfully employed persons according to the Register-Based Labour Market Statistics (RAMS). In order to be classified as ‘gainfully employed’, the person must have earned income exceeding an estimated limit, or have submitted tax returns for business activity during the year concerned. The limit that determines whether or not an employed person is gainfully employed is estimated using a model-based method. The aim is to find a limit value – a level of earned income that, as far as possible, corresponds to the definition of ‘employment’ of the International Labour Organization (ILO). People with earned income that is higher than the limit are assumed to be gainfully employed. The denominator consists of the population. \r\n  \r\nA new source for the self-employed and an adjusted estimation method in RAMS as of the year  2004 causes a break in the time series Aged 20–64 years. \r\n  \r\nSource: [Labour statistics based on administrative sources](https://www.scb.se/am0207-en)"
              ],
              "0000026C": [
                "The numerator consists of the self-employed and business operators with their own limited company. The denominator consists of the number of gainfully employed persons according to the Register-Based Labour Market Statistics (RAMS). Aged 20–64 years.  \r\nSource: [Labour statistics based on administrative sources](https://www.scb.se/am0207-en)"
              ],
              "000001TC": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who sometime during the year have been registered as unemployed according to the register of the Swedish Public Employment Service. A person is defined as being registered as unemployed if during the year they have been registered as openly unemployed and/or job-seeking in programmes with activity support. The denominator consists of the population.  \r\nSource: [STATIV database](https://www.scb.se/STATIV)"
              ],
              "0000026B": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who, sometime during the year, have been registered as openly unemployed in the job-seeking category for open unemployment. As of the 2018 update of new data from 1997 and onwards, the content of Proportion of persons openly unemployed was also adjusted. Previously, it only included persons who, in the past job-seeking period, were registered as openly unemployed. Before the change, a person could only belong to one job-seeking category in the year concerned. The denominator consists of the population. \r\n  \r\nSource: [STATIV](https://www.scb.se/STATIV)"
              ],
              "0000026D": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who, sometime during the year, have been registered as job-seeking in programmes with activity support. The indicator is created by means of grouping the same job-seeking categories used by the Swedish Public Employment Service in its statistics on job-seekers in programmes each year. As of the 2018 update of new data from 1997 and onwards, the content of Proportion of job-seekers in programmes with activity support was also adjusted. Previously, it only included persons who, in the past job-seeking period, were registered as job-seekers in programmes with activity support. Before the change, a person could only belong to one job-seeking category in the year concerned. The denominator consists of the population. \r\n  \r\nSource: [STATIV](https://www.scb.se/STATIV)"
              ],
              "0000026E": [
                "The numerator consists of persons under the age of 25 who are registered as openly unemployed with the Swedish Public Employment Service sometime during the year, for a consecutive period of at least 100 days, and for 25+ years at least six months. The denominator consists of the population. \r\n  \r\nSource: [STATIV](https://www.scb.se/STATIV)"
              ],
              "0000026F": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who are gainfully employed in both year t and year  t-1. The denominator consists of the number of persons who are gainfully employed in year t-1 in each region. Aged 20–64 years in year t. The calculation is only made for persons who are recorded in the population register both years. \r\n  \r\nSource: [Labour statistics based on administrative sources](https://www.scb.se/am0207-en)"
              ],
              "0000026G": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who are business operators in both year t and year  t-1. The denominator consists of the number business operators in year t-1 in each region. The calculation is only made for persons who are recorded in the population register both years. \r\n  \r\nSource: [Population by Labour market status](https://www.scb.se/am0210-en)"
              ],
              "0000026I": [
                "The numerator consists of persons employed in the occupational area managers according to SSYK. The denominator consists of persons who are employed and active and who have a classified occupation.  \r\n  \r\nAs of 2014, occupational data is reported according to the revised Swedish Standard Classification of Occupations (SSYK 2012). SSYK 2012 replaces the previous version, SSYK96. This means that comparisons between 2014 and previous years should not be made. For employees in the 16–64 age range, in 2014 most occupation data, 74 percent, refers to circumstances in the reference year or the following year. 19 percent of the data is imputed using a model that uses the occupation code (according to SSYK 96) that the individual already had in the register. The previous code used may be a maximum of five years old. \r\n Source: [The Swedish Occupational Register with statistics](https://www.scb.se/am0208-en)  \r\nDescription of SSYK: [The Swedish Standard Classification of Occupations 2012 SSYK](https://www.scb.se/ssyk/)  \r\nDescription of gainfully employed: Source: [Population by Labour market status](https://www.scb.se/am0210-en)"
              ],
              "0000026J": [
                "The numerator consists of persons who have post-secondary education and who work in occupational area 2 (occupations requiring advanced level of higher education) and 3 (occupations requiring higher education or equivalent) according to SSYK. The denominator consists of persons who are employed and who have post-secondary education.  \r\n  As of 2014, occupational data is reported according to the revised Swedish Standard Classification of Occupations (SSYK 2012). SSYK 2012 replaces the previous version, SSYK96. This means that comparisons between 2014 and previous years should not be made. For employees in the 16–64 age range, in 2014 most occupation data, 74 percent, refers to circumstances in the reference year or the following year. 19 percent of the data is imputed using a model that uses the occupation code (according to SSYK 96) that the individual already had in the register. The previous code used may be a maximum of five years old. \r\n  \r\nSource: [The Swedish Occupational Register with statistics](https://www.scb.se/am0208-en)  \r\nDescription of SSYK: [The Swedish Standard Classification of Occupations 2012 SSYK](https://www.scb.se/ssyk/)  \r\nDescription of education: [Educational attainment of the population](http://www.scb.se/uf0506-en)  \r\nDescription of gainfully employed: Source: [Population by Labour market status](https://www.scb.se/am0210-en)"
              ],
              "0000026K": [
                "The numerator consist of persons who have post-secondary education and who have employment within qualification levels 3 and 4 according to SSYK2012. The occupational areas that are included in qualification levels 3 and 4 are managerial occupations, occupations requiring an advanced level of higher education or equivalent, and officers in the armed forces occupational area.    The denominator consists of persons who are employed and who have post-secondary education. To be included in the denominator, a person must have an occupation classified according to SSYK2012.  \r\nSource: [The Swedish Occupational Register with statistics](https://www.scb.se/am0208-en).  \r\nDescription of SSYK: [The Swedish Standard Classification of Occupations 2012 SSYK](https://www.scb.se/ssyk/).  \r\nDescription of education: [Educational attainment of the population](http://www.scb.se/uf0506-en).  \r\nDescription of gainfully employed: Source: [Population by Labour market status](https://www.scb.se/am0210-en)."
              ]
            },
